					<personalityDescription>Felix has seen too much to care about petty concerns. He ignores emotions, disregards complaints, and barely acknowledges those he considers beneath him. If someone isn&apos;t immediately useful, they might as well not exist. Felix treats every greeting like a full-scale reunion. Even if he saw you five minutes ago, he&apos;ll wave both arms, slap you on the back, and shout your name like you&apos;ve been missing for years. It&apos;s ridiculous - but in a profession where people do disappear forever, nobody minds hearing, &quot;Well, look who&apos;s still alive! Damn good to see ya!&quot; </personalityDescription>
					<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 52%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Doesn&apos;t see people - just obstacles or irrelevancies.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
