					<personalityDescription>Yazid doesn&apos;t stop - ever. Even when reason, exhaustion, or sheer survival say he should walk away, he grits his teeth and keeps going. He&apos;ll finish what he started, even if it kills him. Yazid&apos;s hands never stop moving - because if they do, he might remember. Remember the times he couldn&apos;t signal for help, when orders were lost in the chaos, when a simple gesture could&apos;ve saved someone but didn&apos;t come in time. He talks with his hands because the alternative is letting them be still - and stillness brings nothing but ghosts. </personalityDescription>
