					<performanceExamScore>45</performanceExamScore>
					<personalityDescription>Enough is never enough for Geraldine. She overcommits, overkills, and overcompensates, whether it&apos;s unloading an entire magazine into a crippled enemy or turning a simple job into an all-consuming mission. If restraint is a virtue, Geraldine never learned it. Geraldine describes her dreams with a sort of detached amusement, like she&apos;s talking about a bad holovid. But the way her hands tighten when she talks about them says otherwise. &quot;Oh, yeah - tentacles, darkness, and the vague sensation that I&apos;m about to dissolve into nothing. You know, normal stuff.&quot; </personalityDescription>
					<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 50%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Overcommits, overkills, overdoes. Restraint is a foreign concept.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
